<h1>Caches</h1>

<p class="page-lead">
  LaTeX-on-HTTP caches fetched resources: when a compilation uses a file that
  was already fetched before (identified by the SHA-256 hash of its content),
  the download is skipped. These endpoints let smart clients inspect and query
  the cache — eg. to avoid re-uploading resources that the server already has.
</p>

